    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305-a1-a6">

                <pb facs="0576" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg556"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fort Lafayette</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">New York Harbor</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-23"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 23, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The board convened pursuant to adjournment.</p>
                <p>Present: Major George W. Wallace, 6th infantry; Major Dickenson Woodruff, 12th
                    infantry; Lieutenant S. W. Cooper, 8th infantry.</p>
                <p>The recorder submitted his report to the board, and, after some modifications, it
                    was adopted<hi rendition="#italic">;</hi> and there being no further business,
                    the board adjourned <hi rendition="#italic">sine die.</hi></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE W. WALLACE, <hi rendition="#italic">Major 6th United States
                            Infantry, President Board.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sidney W. Cooper</hi>,<hi rendition="#italic">
                            Lieutenant 8th Infantry, Recorder.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
